Here I added 10 routers and committed them to areas following OSPF, BGP and RIP protocols programing them to be able to communicate with each other.

!	!!!!!!!!!BGP CONFIG!!!!!!!!!!!!!
!R1
config t
!
interface Loopback0
 ip address 1.1.1.1 255.255.255.0
!
interface Loopback1
 ip address 111.111.111.1 255.255.255.240
!
interface FastEthernet0/0
 ip address 11.11.11.1 255.255.255.0
 duplex auto
 speed auto
!
interface Serial0/0
 ip address 12.12.12.1 255.255.255.240
 clock rate 2000000
!
interface FastEthernet0/1
 no ip address
 shutdown
 duplex auto
 speed auto
!
interface Serial0/1
 ip address 13.13.13.1 255.255.255.240
 clock rate 2000000
!
interface Serial0/2
 no ip address
 shutdown
 clock rate 2000000
!
interface Serial0/3
 no ip address
 shutdown
 clock rate 2000000
!
interface Serial0/4
 no ip address
 shutdown
 clock rate 2000000
!
interface Serial0/5
 ip address 15.15.15.1 255.255.255.240
 clock rate 2000000
!
!
router bgp 100
 no synchronization
 bgp log-neighbor-changes
 network 1.1.1.0 mask 255.255.255.0
 network 11.11.11.0 mask 255.255.255.0
 network 111.111.111.0 mask 255.255.255.240
 neighbor 12.12.12.2 remote-as 200
 neighbor 13.13.13.3 remote-as 100
 neighbor 15.15.15.5 remote-as 56
 no auto-summary
!
!
router rip
  version 2
  no auto-summary
  network 12.12.12.1 
  network 13.13.13.1
  network 11.11.11.1
  network 15.15.15.1
!
end
